1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,653
This is the hardest part of the robot.

2
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:07,833
Not the brain. Not the battery.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:10,156
The actuator.

4
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:16,178
An actuator turns energy into controlled motion.

5
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:19,892
Hydraulics are strong, but heavy.

6
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:23,088
Pneumatics are fast, but springy.

7
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:26,605
Soft actuators are safe, but weak.

8
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,678
Humanoids run on electric motors. Twenty-eight of them.

9
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:38,332
Inside, current flows through copper coils.

10
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:42,515
The field pulls the magnets. The rotor turns.

11
00:00:43,300 --> 00:00:45,033
Torque rises with current.

12
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:48,547
Gears trade speed for force.

13
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:53,358
Encoders read the angle, thousands of times a second.

14
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:59,053
Now, a muscle. Blood cools it. It absorbs shock. It heals.

15
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:04,290
Copper only heats. Double the torque, four times the heat.

16
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:07,246
Every joint is a trade.

17
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:11,694
More torque needs more mass. More mass needs more torque.

18
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:14,936
Push hard, and motors overheat.

19
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:18,367
Land a jump, and the gears take the blow.

20
00:01:19,100 --> 00:01:21,978
Gear down, and the joint loses its feel.

21
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:26,729
Now build millions. Precise. Durable. Cheap.

22
00:01:27,600 --> 00:01:31,410
Intelligence can be copied. Muscle must be manufactured.

23
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,863
Solve the actuator, and everything changes.

24
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:40,850
Machines that move like we do.

25
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:46,930
The brain is ready.

26
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:50,676
The body is still being built.
